      "id": "claim_f68c63f7c95e4bae97d40b24437b19db",
      "statement": "prohibitAllSharing is the blunt stopgap: a gatekeeper marking an observation prohibitAllSharing throws when the workspace already has shares, otherwise the flag latches into lockdown (no further sharing, no web fetches); it cannot express 'shareable only with people who also have access', which is what the per-user observer mechanism adds.",
